{
  "description": "What a FULL queue does with a new event (REQ-DLV-007, REQ-DLV-009). queue is the queue, oldest first, with the class of each event; new is the event that arrives. The rule: (1) a new critical event displaces the OLDEST queued event of class bulk, or when there is none the OLDEST one of class normal, with the reason displaced_by_critical; the new event takes the last place. (2) When it displaces nothing (a non-critical event, or a critical one with no lower class queued) the policy decides: drop_newest drops the new event (reason queue_full_newest); drop_oldest displaces the oldest queued event whose class is not higher than the class of the new one (reason queue_full_oldest, the new event takes the last place) and, when there is none, drops the new event (queue_full_newest); block_with_timeout answers wait (nothing changes now; if no room appears within the timeout the new event is dropped with the reason block_timeout). outcome is drop_new, displace or wait; removed lists the events taken out of the queue with their reason; queue_after is the order of the ids after the case (the new event has id 100) and reason is the reason of the decision. The order of the events that stay is kept. The class order is bulk < normal < critical.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "drop_newest_drops_the_new_normal",
      "description": "With drop_newest a new normal event is dropped, whatever the queue holds.",
      "policy": "drop_newest",
      "queue": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "class": "normal"
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "class": "normal"
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "class": "bulk"
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "class": "normal"
        }
      ],
      "new": {
        "id": 100,
        "class": "normal"
      },
      "expected": {
        "outcome": "drop_new",
        "removed": [],
        "queue_after": [
          1,
          2,
          3,
          4
        ],
        "reason": "queue_full_newest"
      }
    },
    {
